# The resolver half of `dns` needs a DNS resolver, which this profile does not
# have. Node's `resolve*`, `Resolver`, `setServers` and `getServers` go through
# c-ares (`deps/cares`); `lookup` and `lookupService` go through the platform's
# `getaddrinfo`/`getnameinfo`, which this profile does have as a `net` binding.
#
# Those are two capabilities behind one module name, and only one of them is
# present. The files below need the other. They are named individually rather
# than excluded by a pattern, so that adding c-ares later is a list to work
# through rather than a rule to remember to delete.
test-dns-cancel-reverse-lookup.js: needs c-ares; this profile resolves through the platform's getaddrinfo and has no DNS client of its own. `resolve*`, `Resolver`, `setServers` and `getServers` all go through node's `deps/cares` and none of them has a getaddrinfo equivalent -- they speak the wire protocol and deliberately ignore /etc/hosts, which is behaviour rather than an implementation detail
